tient care. Additionally, it encompasses the clinical presentation of infections associated with catheters, detailing symptoms and diagnostic criteria for sepsis and other related complications. This dual focus highlights the importance of both nutritional support and infection management within clinical settings.", "HEMOCULTIVOS:Hemocultures are tests used to detect the presence of bacteria or fungi in the blood, crucial for diagnosing bacteremia related to catheters.", "ANTIBIOTERAPIA:Antibioterapia refers to the treatment of infections through the use of antibiotics. This therapy may be tailored according to culture results to ensure effective management of the infection. Additionally, antibiotic therapy is essential in addressing complications that may arise from intestinal failure, highlighting its critical role in both infection management and the treatment of related health issues.", "OSTEOMIELITIS:Osteomyelitis is an infection in the bone that can occur as a complication of severe infections related to central venous catheters.", "NEUTROPENIA:Neutropenia is a medical condition characterized by low levels of neutrophils, a type of white blood cell essential for fighting off infections. This condition leads to an increased susceptibility to infections, particularly in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type Ib (GSDIb). Additionally, the low neutrophil count associated with neutropenia can influence dietary choices due to the heightened risk of infections. Neutropenia can occur in individuals with GSDIb, further complicating their health management.", "C. GALBRATA:C. Galbrata is a contributor to the bibliographic references related to pediatric radiology and thrombolytic therapy in children.", "LA FE DEPARTAMENT DE SALUT:La Fe Departament de Salut is a healthcare organization involved in nutritional diagnosis and follow-up protocols.", "VALENCIANA:Valenciana refers to the region associated with the La Fe healthcare facility.", "PROTOCOLO DE DIAGNÓSTICO Y SEGUIMIENTO NUTRICIONAL DE LA DISFAGIA:The \"PROTOCOLO DE DIAGNÓSTICO Y SEGUIMIENTO NUTRICIONAL DE LA DISFAGIA\" is a comprehensive protocol designed for the diagnosis and monitoring of dysphagia. It details specific procedures and assessments aimed at ensuring safe swallowing for patients experiencing this condition. The protocol not only focuses on the diagnostic aspects but also emphasizes the importance of nutritional follow-up for individuals with dysphagia. It provides guidelines for safe eating practices, ensuring that patients receive appropriate recommendations to manage their condition effectively. Overall, this protocol serves as a crucial resource for healthcare professionals in the assessment and ongoing care of dysphagia patients.", "OWEN A:Owen A is an author of a study on malfunctioning central venous catheters in children.", "ROEBUCK D:Roebuck D is an author of a study on malfunctioning central venous catheters in children.", "HIORNS M:Hiorns M is an author of a study on malfunctioning central venous catheters in children.", "BASKIN J:Baskin J is an author of a study on the management of occlusion and thrombosis associated with long-term indwelling central venous catheters."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}